course: dictionary
lesson: 1301
title: One word, three meanings
level: primary-6
stars: 0
explain: A word can have more than one meaning, and the context tells you which one is meant. Byzantine with a capital B is a name in history: «The Byzantine Empire» was the eastern part of the Roman Empire, with its capital at Constantinople, now Istanbul.
explain: In art and church lessons, Byzantine describes gold mosaics, domes and holy pictures called icons. «The Byzantine emperor Justinian built the great church of Hagia Sophia with its huge dome.» The sentence is about history and a building, so Byzantine names the empire.
explain: With a small b, byzantine is a formal word meaning far too complicated and hard to understand. «The rules were so byzantine that nobody could follow them.» Ask: is the sentence talking about a place, a picture or a system? Then choose the meaning that fits.
fact: Byzantine (capital B) describes the Byzantine Empire, the eastern part of the Roman Empire.
fact: The Byzantine Empire lasted about a thousand years after Rome fell, with its capital at Constantinople, now Istanbul.
fact: «Istanbul was Constantinople, the Byzantine capital, which the Ottomans conquered in 1453.»
fact: Byzantine art has gold mosaics, domes and holy pictures called icons.
fact: byzantine (small b) means far too complicated and hard to understand, like «byzantine rules».
exercise: «The Ottoman sultan Mehmed II captured Constantinople in 1453, ending the Byzantine Empire.» What was the Byzantine Empire? | *The eastern part of the Roman Empire, with its capital at Constantinople | A type of gold mosaic | A set of rules that is hard to follow | A modern country in South America
exercise: «Byzantine art has gold mosaics, domes and holy pictures called icons.» What are icons? | Gold coins used in shops | *Holy pictures | Tall towers for watching the sea | Small boats used on rivers
exercise: «The rules for the forms were so byzantine that nobody could follow them.» What does byzantine mean here? | Very old, from ancient Rome | Made of gold and glass | Quick and simple | *Far too complicated and hard to understand
test: «The Byzantine emperor Justinian built the great church of Hagia Sophia.» Here, what does Byzantine mean? | A word for something far too complicated | *A name in history, the Byzantine Empire | A type of silk | A kind of icon for sale
test: «Mehmed II captured Constantinople in 1453.» What is Constantinople called today? | Rome | Athens | *Istanbul | Venice
exam: Mia reads «The byzantine rules confused everyone» and says byzantine means old and golden. Which is right? | Big and round like a dome | *Far too complicated and hard to understand | Old and golden, like Byzantine art | A name for a kind of cake
